steam-arm-setup (3.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Run report: Maintenance, Report how last game ran, or steam-arm-config
    report run; one file per game start, allow-listed lines only, shown
    before saving; nothing leaves machine.
  * Run history, off by default: one line per start and end of x86 game
    through emulation in client folder .local/state/steam-arm/runs.log.
  * Automatic tuning, off by default, per game (title key autotune=fix,
    Games menu or steam-arm-config tune): verdict per start from time,
    CPU use and renderer check; after bad start next start tries one
    changed setting (graphics route, FEX Multiblock, 32-bit GL
    forwarding); at most 4 trials per stamp; results in tuned.conf of
    client home, below title profiles; never sends signal to game. Line
    with tuning evidence but no decision state counts as result.
  * --detect and launcher log name state of each own fix (patch lines);
    retired fixes are not applied.
  * Launch handler of native client enters through stand-in of Valve's
    launch wrapper; Valve's FEX tool files stay unedited; FEX tool edit
    stays as fallback.
  * Game-only settings of native client (vk-spoof layer on, shader-cache
    layer off) go into Valve's game environment file
    ~/.config/steam/env/gfx.txt of client home as marked block; lines
    written by hand kept; removal takes block out. Settings that launch
    options override per title stay in launcher environment.
  * FEX-2610 tool and newer: code cache on for every title by Valve;
    diskcache=off turns it off per title.
  * Setup no longer links root filesystem as /usr/share/guestos/fex-mesa;
    link of earlier versions removed.
  * Title profile layers: included, automatic tuning results, system,
    personal.
  * Issue forms ask for one Steam ARM report field.
  * Renderer check no longer reports CPU drawing for game that waits or
    stops before drawing; CPU verdict needs busy game.
  * Removal with --purge deletes empty folders setup made; box64 binfmt
    shell error and missing udev rules folder fixed.
  * Extra Mesa versions for route B games, none by default (Components,
    Driver archive, Extra versions, or --mesa-extra with
    --mesa-extra-file): one tree per SHA-256 pinned version; title key
    mesa=<version> picks it per game; route A: log line only.
  * --detect line official client: none|found, detection only.

