steam-arm-setup (2.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Renderer check: handler logs whether title draws on GPU or on CPU
    (llvmpipe); STEAM_ARM_RENDERER_CHECK=0 turns it off.
  * Page size in settings menu title bar and in setup and removal banners.
  * FEX build matches CPU: fex-emu-armv8.0, -armv8.2 or -armv8.4; setup
    on ARMv8.0 CPUs (Cortex-A72) no longer stops.
  * Display mode restore after titles and when Steam closes;
    STEAM_ARM_MODE_RESTORE=0 turns it off.
  * steam-arm --shutdown, with SIGTERM fallback; interface switch uses it.
  * MangoHud in 64-bit x86 Linux titles: library copied from root
    filesystem into client folder and preloaded from there.
  * kde-input-prompt component, off by default; profile key multiblock.
  * Compatibility tool and GoldSrc log lines; Information shows OpenGL
    and CPU governor per cluster.
  * Restore keeps Proton choice made now. Menu: restore summary button
    Next; wizard Back no longer skips Vulkan screen.
  * Launcher keeps host Bluetooth adapter on: writes adapter state to
    System/Bluetooth/Enabled in config.vdf, powers it on at exit when
    client left it off.
  * Armv8.1 check: setup and launcher stop on CPUs without LSE atomics
    (steam-for-linux #13288); STEAM_ARM_ALLOW_ARMV80=1 skips it.
  * First start: desktop notification reports client download; menu
    icons show plain disc until client's own icon file arrives.
  * FEX version read from FEXGetConfig --version (FEX-2608 and newer
    have no FEXInterpreter).
  * steam:// links open in Steam ARM (x-scheme-handler/steam). Update /
    Repair asks Run / Back first; kde-input-prompt label fits checklist.
  * Setup started from folder game user cannot enter (/root) no longer
    stops with "client program missing after unpacking".

